remoteok.json is RECONSTRUCTED from the public API's documented shape
(https://remoteok.com/api), not a live capture: the container that wrote it had
no network. The payload is a bare JSON array, so it cannot carry a "_comment"
key of its own; this file says it instead.

Contents: the legal notice element first (where the live API serves it), two
valid postings (one with a string id and salaries, one with a numeric id and
the zero/empty salaries that mean "not stated"), and one malformed entry with
no "position".

Re-record it on the first live run.
